+//! Issue #696 (child 2 of 3 of the #681 split, proposal 0016 decision 7(e)): rebalance
+//! resolves every committed object the way every other consumer already resolves one,
+//! contains per object what it cannot read, and refuses — rather than aborts or silently
+//! discards — the evacuation it does not own.
+//!
+//! On the base, `rebalance.rs` `?`-s out on `ChunkMapError::SegmentedMapUnsupported` at both
+//! of its chunk-map reads, so ONE segmented object anywhere stops every drain in the store:
+//! no server can be decommissioned once a single multipart object exists.
+//!
+//! Every leg drives the REAL fenced control point
+//! [`reconcile_step`](wyrd_custodian::reconcile_step) over one shared `MemMeta` double, never
+//! an internal helper, and no assertion names a symbol this patch introduces: the red leg
+//! reverts `rebalance.rs`, so a new symbol would fail to COMPILE rather than fail an
+//! assertion.
+//!
+//! Legs 1-6 are that base red — leg 5 included, one leg MORE than the brief's
+//! `Falsifiability` predicted, and deliberately so. Leg 5 binds the containment against
+//! OVER-breadth (a guard that refuses a segmented object holding NOTHING on a draining
+//! server withholds every decommission, this slice's own defect mirrored), and there is no
+//! way to assert what the pass ANSWERS over a store the base cannot walk at all without
+//! failing on the base too: the honest choices are a leg that is red here or a leg that
+//! asserts nothing anywhere. Leg 7 is the one deliberately non-red leg — a fault that is
+//! not one object's map still ends the pass, which the base does as well.
+//!
+//! Leg 3 carries two sub-assertions beside its own: Rule C (a record under `inode:007` is
+//! never silently reinterpreted into `inode:7`), and the row this pass may not ADDRESS —
+//! `inode:foo`, named and refused, never evacuated and CAS'd back where no reader looks.
+
+#![forbid(unsafe_code)]
+
+use std::collections::{BTreeMap, HashMap};
+use std::sync::{Arc, Mutex, Once};
+
+use async_trait::async_trait;
+use bytes::Bytes;
+use tracing::instrument::WithSubscriber;
+use wyrd_coordination_mem::MemCoordination;
+use wyrd_core::metadata::{
+    decode, encode, inode_key, resolve_chunk_map, seg_key, ChunkMap, ChunkRef, EcScheme,
+    InodeRecord, InodeState, SegmentGroup, SegmentRecord, SegmentRef, SegmentedMap,
+};
+use wyrd_core::placement::Topology;
+use wyrd_core::write::{plan_write, write_fragments};
+use wyrd_custodian::desired_state::{set_lifecycle, DServerLifecycle::Draining};
+use wyrd_custodian::{
